noah-cs: Heads up — Ledgerly onboarding hit a webhook replay that created a retry storm and spiked our preflight 429s. Customer ran their test harness and replayed delivery events ~11:05 UTC.

ariel-cs: How many retries and from what IPs/agents? Any Retry-After seen?

noah-cs: From their support dump: repeated POSTs to /v1/preflight from the same host with short spacing. Server log excerpt: 
```
[11:05:12] POST /v1/preflight 200
[11:05:13] POST /v1/preflight 429 x-retry-after: 25
[11:05:13] POST /v1/preflight 429 x-retry-after: 25
[11:05:14] POST /v1/preflight 429 x-retry-after: 25
```
Also their connector emitted immediate retries on 4xx/5xx without honoring Retry-After.

sam-eng: That explains it — if client doesn't back off on Retry-After you get a tight fanout. Two things: (1) short-term, we can enable a per-endpoint rate-shed rule to add jitter on repeats from same IP for 30m; (2) recommend patch: honor Retry-After header and add an exponential backoff with jitter.

maria-sre: I can deploy a temporary rule for org ledgerly-testing-3 to gate identical preflight requests with a 250ms randomized delay on identical path+org. Need org_id and region to scope.

noah-cs: org_id=ledgerly-testing-3, region=eu-central-1. Customer also asked if we can silence alerts while they patch since this is a test replay.

webhook-bot: :warning: Policy change queued by maria-sre  apply-per-org-slowdown ledgerly-testing-3 ttl=45m change-id=policy-2026-10-04-0042

ariel-cs: Can we draft a short onboarding note for connectors: "When replaying events do not parallelize preflight/exchange; serialize or reuse session tokens; honor Retry-After" and include a sample backoff snippet?

sam-eng: Sample Node backoff we recommend: 
```js
async function sendWithBackoff(req){
  let delay = 300;
  for(let i=0;i<5;i++){
    const res = await fetch(req);
    if(res.status===200) return res;
    const ra = res.headers.get('x-retry-after') || res.headers.get('Retry-After');
    if(ra) delay = Math.max(delay, parseInt(ra)*1000 + Math.random()*200);
    await sleep(delay);
    delay = Math.min(5000, delay*1.6 + Math.random()*100);
  }
  throw new Error('failed after retries');
}
```

noah-cs: Customer patched their harness to serialize replays and honor Retry-After. Post-patch their preflight errors dropped to near-zero within 6 minutes. They appreciated the temporary rule.

ariel-cs: Great — please add an onboarding checklist item: "Are you running event replays or connector test harnesses? If yes, ask them to throttle replays or request a temporary grace window."

maria-sre: Done. I've also flagged a dashboard panel to show replay-origin hits so CSMs can surface this early. Closing thread after doc PR. :white_check_mark:
